I now have sufficient independent verification to issue a verdict. Let me compile my findings.

**Independent verification summary:**
- Motus camera score: ✓ 21.6% on RoboTwin 2.0-Plus Table 3 confirmed
- OA-WAM camera score on LIBERO-Plus: ✓ 80.5% confirmed from HTML fetch of 2605.06481v1
- Being-H0.7 K=16 latent queries: ✓ confirmed from HTML fetch of 2605.00078v1
- Being-H0.7 RoboTwin 2.0 domain randomization excludes camera viewpoint: ✓ confirmed (only clutter/lighting/background/height/language)
- ReViWo ICLR 2025: ✓ confirmed, code at github.com/lafmdp/ReViWo
- Motus public weights: ✓ confirmed at motus-robotics/Motus on HuggingFace
- **NEW FINDING**: RoboTwin 2.0-Plus is described as "in-house" by the arXiv:2603.22078 authors (Huawei/UToronto), constructed on top of RoboTwin 2.0 with LIBERO-Plus perturbation protocol. The evaluation code is **not confirmed publicly available** — no GitHub link found for the Plus variant

